  "guide": {
    "order": [
      "1. server_info and twin_catalog: read the kinds, frames, mounts, series, tones, limits and this guide.",
      "2. Read the photos. Write your reading list in chat: stations, devices, what is fastened to what, directions, labels.",
      "3. twin_scene_draft {scene, draft} with the SKELETON: schema 2 devices with on, mount, pose, params, io, timing and a basis word (label, ref, guess; measured and user only for what the person gave) for each number you give. No skin yet. The reply has facts, ask, notes, not_simulated, limits.",
      "4. Compare facts with your reading list. Put the ask items to the person (mounts, bores and strokes that are guesses, one measured reference length: scene key refs). Correct the skeleton and draft again.",
      "5. twin_scene_draft again with the same scene plus a skin (and indicators) on the devices. The server saves skin_source model; only the person can set it to checked on the page.",
      "6. twin_render to look at the result and compare it with the photos.",
      "7. The person adjusts places and travels on the page and confirms the draft. You write only the draft."
    ],
    "workpieces": "Workpieces (schema 2, simulation only; rules, no physics). 1. Read the photo (twin_photo_get) and the tones of `tones`. 2. Draft scene key `workpieces.types` {name: {shape round|square, d_mm or side_mm, h_mm, material metal|plastic, tone (a name of tones except mark), basis}}: one type for each shape, colour and size; sizes from a known length are basis ref, by eye guess; write material as you think and always basis guess, because a photo does not show metal. 3. Draft scene key `points` [{name (1-24 of a-z 0-9 _), on (\"<id>\" or \"<id>.<frame>\": the device that makes or holds the part there, so the point moves with it), pos [x,y,z] in that frame (the bottom centre of a part that rests there), catch_mm, holds, basis}]. 4. Device keys: `stack` {point, fed_by (a cylinder with a push rule from that point), content (type names, lowest first, at most 20), refill}; `push` [{from, to}] on a cylinder (at most 4); `stop` {at} on a conveyor or {belt, at} on a cylinder (active from half stroke); `sense` on a sensor, exactly one of {point, within_mm, material any|metal}, {held_by: a pad or gripper}, {pulse_of: a conveyor, mm_per_pulse}; `position` {from (D, W, R, ZR word or U<n>\\G<n>), width 16|32, per_mm, speed_mm_s} on a servo_axis; scene key `workpieces.start` [{type, at}] and `modules` (a QD77MS model, same form as scenario.modules of ladder_from_il). 5. Read facts.points, facts.workpieces, facts.push (contact_mm and end_gap_mm of each push rule) and ask: put the ask lines to the person (which colour is metal, one puck measured with a ruler), then draft again with basis user or measured. The person confirms the draft on the page. Limits: 32 points, 8 types, 20 start parts, 4 stacks, 16 push rules, 8 stops, 32 sensor rules, 50 parts at the start.",
    "skin_rules": "A skin is the look only: {groups:[{name (1-16 of a-z 0-9 _), frame (a frame of the same device, default base), show|hide (a bit address that an io slot or a bit signal of a device of the scene has), items:[{t:box,size,pos,rot,tone}|{t:cyl,d,len,d2,axis,pos,rot,tone}]}]}. Items are in the coordinates of the frame of their group; a group on `out` moves with the rod, a group on `carriage` with the carriage. tone is one of `tones`; `mark` only in a group with `show`. At most 16 groups, 64 items and 16384 bytes for each device, 1000 skin items for the scene. A skin sets no size, place, travel, direction, address or timing: those are the skeleton. `indicators` shows the bits of other devices on a board: [{from (first bit address), count (1-64), at [x,y,z], step [dx,dy,dz], frame, d}], at most 8 rows and 128 lamps for each device.",
    "skin_recipe": {
      "note": "A lamp that the PLC drives is a device of kind lamp. Its look is two groups of one address: the dark lamp while the bit is OFF, the lit lamp (tone mark) while it is ON.",
      "device": {
        "id": "l1", "kind": "lamp", "io": {"coil": "Y10"},
        "skin": {"groups": [
          {"name": "lamp_off", "hide": "Y10", "items": [{"t": "cyl", "d": 14, "len": 6, "axis": "y", "pos": [0, 3, 0], "tone": "dark"}]},
          {"name": "lamp_on", "show": "Y10", "items": [{"t": "cyl", "d": 14, "len": 6, "axis": "y", "pos": [0, 3, 0], "tone": "mark"}]}
        ]}
      }
    }
  },
  "series": {
    "generic": {"source": "Assumed ratios of the design study (docs/research/photo-twin/10-architecture.md 2.5): body_len 3.0 * bore + stroke (never below stroke + 20), body_dia 1.4 * bore, rod_dia 0.4 * bore, rod_out 2.0 * bore, pivot_back 1.5 * bore. No maker table; values marked ratio."},
    "smc_cm2": {
      "source": "SMC CM2 series, CAT.EUS20-269A-UK, page 8 Basic (Double-side Bossed) (B): S, I, D, H; page 12 Single Clevis (C): L (design 10-architecture.md 2.5). cylinder_single adds 25 mm to S for each started 50 mm of stroke (CAT.EUS20-269B-UK page 37). CDM2 (built-in magnet) is taken to have the same sizes: not verified.",
      "spring_mm_per_50": 25,
      "bores": {
        "20": {"S": 62, "I": 28, "D": 8, "H": 41, "L": 30},
        "25": {"S": 62, "I": 33.5, "D": 10, "H": 45, "L": 30},
        "32": {"S": 64, "I": 37.5, "D": 12, "H": 45, "L": 30},
        "40": {"S": 88, "I": 46.5, "D": 14, "H": 50, "L": 39}
      }
    }
  },
  "layout_note": "Millimetres, y is up, y = 0 is the floor. A device pose.pos is the bottom centre of the device. Each part has size [x,y,z] and pos = offset of the part's bottom centre from the device pose.pos (override with the device `parts` field: {part: {pos, rot}}). A port `at` is the offset from the bottom centre of its part. A cylinder lies along x. Rotation is about y (pose.rot[1]). Parts are static: a stroke is not part of the size. Put devices on the floor (pos y 0) or on top of another device, keep boxes from overlapping, and draw air links valve_a -> cap and valve_b -> rod (a device with a valve and no links gets these by default).",
